                <pb facs="0462" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363/860: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-16T14:00:00+03:25">June 16, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 16—1:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>432. From Leavell. Any assistance that could be rendered to Curtice and Hoover in
                    advancing their priorities would be exceedingly helpful in the negotiations here
                    as negotiations are at a standstill until their arrival and the American
                    position is steadily deteriorating for reasons mentioned in previous wires and
                    the fear by Iranians that London negotiations may either divide the territory
                    between Americans and British or turn it over to the British. Please cable if
                    Sinclair have delivered final bid in their name to Hoover and Curtice. If they
                    have failed to do so it would appear on information gathered here that they are
                    delaying matters in order to learn what the other bidders for the concession
                    have submitted which information can be secured through leaks here. Any
                    instructions as to policy to be followed here would be greatly appreciated.</p>
                <p>Believe concession can still be had for American company if no delays by Sinclair
                    and if concession does not get entangled in Millspaugh Mission controversy.
                    [Leavell.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
